            <ArticleTitle>Use of ketamine for refractory wheezing in an infant.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>587-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ketamine has bronchodilator properties and is used for severe bronchospasm in adults and children with asthma. Here, we report successful use of ketamine in a young infant with bronchospasm.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
